# NOTICE

`AbstractSymbology.ili` is unmodified, fetched from
`https://models.interlis.ch/refhb24/AbstractSymbology.ili` (the official
INTERLIS models catalog - openly published for reuse). Not actually
needed by `RasterSign` itself (a standalone class, no abstract base), kept
alongside `StandardSymbology_ext.ili` only because it was copied from the
same source directory as `roadsexgm2ien_repo/` - harmless, not imported
by anything that matters here.

`StandardSymbology_ext.ili` is an ADAPTED copy of
`https://models.interlis.ch/refhb24/StandardSymbology.ili` -
**not the official model**. It renames `MODEL StandardSymbology` to
`StandardSymbologyRasterSignExt` (so it is never confused with, or
accidentally loaded alongside, the real one, or the separate
`FontSymbol_Image` extension in `../fontsymbol_image_repo/`) and adds one
project-proposed extension: `STRUCTURE RasterColorMapEntry` (`Value`/
`Color`/`Label`) and `CLASS RasterSign` (`ColorMapEntries: LIST OF
RasterColorMapEntry`) - a raster/coverage styling proposal covering only
a value->color ramp so far, matching `pycartosym`'s `Symbolizer.color_map`
(confirmed to write a real `se:CoverageStyle/se:RasterSymbolizer/
se:ColorMap`). Proposed and validated by the maintainer 2026-09-13.
Channel selection and hill-shading are not built yet. No other content
was changed.

`../rastersign_example.ili`/`.xtf` are hand-built synthetic fixtures
(same convention as `pycartosym_examples.ili` - only the `.xtf` wire
shape matters, `SignLibrary` never reads the built schema) exercising
`RasterSign`/`Sign := {name}` end to end - no real `.xtf` can exist yet
for a class this project just proposed.
